# CODEOWNERS
# Paths are matched from the repository root. The last matching pattern wins.
#
# `@DipDevDevelopers` is the organisation's developers team and is the owner below. It
# resolves to real people, which is the whole point: a CODEOWNERS rule naming a handle
# that does not exist provides no protection while looking exactly like it does. That is
# why `@dip-develop` — the organisation login, which is not a team and not a user — is
# gone from this file. Required code-owner review is enabled on both protected branches,
# so these entries are load-bearing from now on.
#
# Rename the team and every line below has to change with it.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
/*                       @DipDevDevelopers

# Specification and architecture: changes here change the contract for every package.
/docs/                   @DipDevDevelopers
/ARCHITECTURE.md         @DipDevDevelopers

# Security-sensitive material. Treat every PR touching these as security-relevant: a
# reviewer other than the author is already required, and these paths are why.
/SECURITY.md                            @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/security/                         @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/extensibility/plugins.md          @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/extensibility/tools.md            @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/extensibility/injections.md       @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/decisions/risks.md                @DipDevDevelopers

# Compatibility surfaces: protocol framing, config schema, error and exit codes.
/docs/architecture/protocol.md          @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/architecture/configuration.md     @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/reference/                        @DipDevDevelopers

# Release, signing and automation. The install root, the launcher and the runtime
# verification order are security-relevant: a change here decides what executes.
/.github/workflows/                     @DipDevDevelopers
/.github/dependabot.yml                 @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/architecture/install-and-update.md @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/architecture/build-and-release.md @DipDevDevelopers

# The project website. Separate from the product on purpose: it resolves its own
# toolchain, sits outside the pub workspace, and is never part of a release.
/site/                                 @DipDevDevelopers
/docs/website.md                       @DipDevDevelopers

# # The lockfile is committed deliberately: one reviewer, no drive-by updates.
/pubspec.lock                           @DipDevDevelopers

# The recorded repository settings. A change here is a change to branch protection or the
# label set, which is why it is reviewed rather than re-recorded on a whim.
/repo-settings.json                     @DipDevDevelopers
